# --- HTTP API ---
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development

# --- CORS ---
# The browser-reachable origin the frontend is actually served from (never a Docker
# Compose-internal hostname) — see main.ts's own comment for the full reasoning.
FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3001

# --- PostgreSQL (added in Phase 2) ---
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://payroll:payroll@localhost:5432/payroll?schema=public

# --- Redis / BullMQ (added in Phase 4) ---
REDIS_HOST=localhost
REDIS_PORT=6379

# --- Simulated payroll provider (added in Phase 5) ---
# SimulatedPayrollProvider (backend/src/processing/simulated-payroll-provider.ts) is fully
# deterministic — no randomness, no artificial latency, no env-configurable failure rates. It
# succeeds unless `employeeId` contains one of two reserved marker substrings
# (FORCE_PROVIDER_FAILURE / FORCE_PROVIDER_TRANSIENT_FAILURE), which force a permanent or
# transient failure respectively. There is nothing to configure here.
